    "title": "How to watch Celtics vs. Thunder today: Time, TV channel",
    "text": "March 12, 2026, 6:02 a.m. CTThe Oklahoma City Thunder will host the Boston Celtics on Thursday. This will be the first matchup of the season between the two squads.The Thunder (51-15) had a blockbuster 129-126 win over the Denver Nuggets on Monday. Shai Gilgeous-Alexander stamped his MVP case with 35 points and 15 assists. He hit the game-winner on a stepback 3-pointer.Meanwhile, the Celtics (43-22) couldn't overcome Jaylen Brown's early ejection in a 125-116 loss to the San Antonio Spurs on Tuesday. Derrick White had 34 points and seven assists against his old squad.Here's how to watch the Thunder's game, including time, TV schedule and streaming information:What channel is Celtics vs. Thunder game on today? Time, TV scheduleTV Channel: Amazon Prime, FanDuel Sports Network OklahomaStart time: 8:30 p.m. CTWhere to watch Celtics vs. Thunder on livestreamWatch Celtics vs. Thunder live on Amazon PrimeCeltics vs. Thunder injury updatesThunder: Jalen Williams (hamstring strain) is out. Isaiah Hartenstein (calf contusion) is out. Nikola Topic (G League assignment) is out. Branden Carlson (back strain) is out. Thomas Sorber (torn ACL) is out.Celtics: Jayson Tatum (Achilles repair reconditioning) is questionable. Derrick White (knee contusion) is questionable. Nikola Vucevic (finger fracture) is out. Payton Pritchard (back spasm) is probable. Baylor Scheierman (thumb fracture) is available. John Tonje (G League two-way) is out.Oklahoma City ThunderShai Gilgeous-AlexanderCason WallaceLu DortJaylin WilliamsChet HolmgrenBoston CelticsPayton PritchardBaylor ScheiermanJaylen BrownSam HauserNeemias QuetaCeltics vs. Thunder predictions, picks, oddsThunder 113, Celtics 107: The Thunder will need to keep pace with the red-hot Spurs. That means it's the time to beat the Celtics at home. Depending on Tatum and White, the difficulty level might be notched down. Gilgeous-Alexander will get a chance to break Wilt Chamberlain's 20-point streak. Expect him to. On top of that, OKC should get a resume win over Boston to not spoil the historic achievement. The Celtics might be the best team in the East, but the Thunder and Spurs are just on another level.ODDS: Thunder by 6.5 pointsO/U: 215.5All NBA Odds via BetMGM.Thunder 2025-26 scheduleSunday, Mar. 15 vs. TimberwolvesTuesday, Mar. 17 at MagicWednesday, Mar. 18 at NetsWe occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
